    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output today, headlined by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (73.76), and **Kyle Tucker** (71.13). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is our premier start; he faces the vulnerable Ethan Pecko (5.95 xERA), and the combination of a favorable park shift and a strong #3-hole lineup placement makes him the cornerstone of today\u2019s production. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a high-leverage #2 spot against Seth Lugo, while **Kyle Tucker** remains an elite-tier play due to his consistent ability to rack up counting stats even in neutral matchups. **Heliot Ramos** (68.16) rounds out our top-tier recommendations, capitalizing on the same soft matchup against Pecko to provide significant value in the outfield.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Sam Antonacci** (43.60), who fell just shy of the 44-point threshold required to displace **Drake Baldwin** (44.10) or **Jackson Merrill** (49.36). While **Sam Antonacci** benefits from a strong projected #1-hole advantage, his matchup against the elite Jacob deGrom (3.05 xERA) significantly hampered his outlook, ultimately pushing the optimizer to favor the higher raw-base projections of our active starters. We are also keeping a close eye on **Jackson Merrill**, who is running into a formidable test against Paul Skenes; while his score of 49.36 is solid, the matchup against an elite arm and his designation as a high-risk hold for SB efficiency keeps his ceiling somewhat compressed today.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given that many of our scores are tethered to \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions. Specifically, **Liam Hicks** (57.48) and **Coby Mayo** (48.39) occupy vital slots, but their overall utility could fluctuate if their real-world batting orders drop further down the lineup than our current projections. **Andy Pages** remains sidelined on the IL, and while we have deep bench coverage with players like **Miguel Vargas** and **Dominic Smith**, their sub-40 scores against difficult arms like deGrom and Glasnow correctly relegate them to the bench to preserve our game caps. With elite pitching matchups scattered across the slate, we are prioritizing high-efficiency spots to maintain our Roto edge.",
